{"component_id_namespace":"ec077a53-0b40-5f21-b1fe-a62094d2476b","component_schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","components":[{"attributes":{"code":"TMC","legacy_node_id":"ks-topeka:tmc:17.30.250","page_type":"section"},"citation":"17.30.250","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/17.30.250","content_hash":"5c2c2cdb0d55e6360b474e63e0854613726466a5e73ec7bcd50e733672ac717a","heading":"Floodplain management variance criteria.","ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":null,"schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:17.30.250:section","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/17.30.250","text":"In passing upon such applications for variances, the Board shall consider all technical data and evaluations, all relevant factors, standards specified in other sections of this chapter, and the following criteria:\n(a) Danger to life and property due to flood damage;\n(b) Danger that materials may be swept onto other lands to the injury of others;\n(c) Susceptibility of the proposed facility and its contents to flood damage and the effect of such damage on the individual owner;\n(d) Importance of the services provided by the proposed facility to the community;\n(e) Necessity to the facility of a waterfront location, where applicable;\n(f) Availability of alternative locations, not subject to flood damage, for the proposed use;\n(g) Compatibility of the proposed use with existing and anticipated development;\n(h) Relationship of the proposed use to the comprehensive plan and floodplain management program for that area;\n(i) Safety of access to the property in times of flood for ordinary and emergency vehicles;\n(j) Expected heights, velocity, duration, rate of rise and sediment transport of the flood waters, if applicable, expected at the site; and\n(k) Costs of providing governmental services during and after flood conditions, including maintenance and repair of public utilities and facilities such as sewer, gas, electrical, and water systems; streets; and bridges. (Ord. 20425 § 14, 6-20-23.)\nCross References: Board of Zoning Appeals, TMC 2.220.010 .","type":"section","workbench_component_id":"df41e4ec-246b-5f54-b23b-8c1525792cd9"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"17.30.250","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/17.30.250","content_hash":"23a80f636c62745f6e8f0c89be5c07dae6f6b88db7e65e79f6b1962d99054ebf","heading":null,"ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:17.30.250:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:17.30.250:block:0","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/17.30.250","text":"In passing upon such applications for variances, the Board shall consider all technical data and evaluations, all relevant factors, standards specified in other sections of this chapter, and the following criteria:","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"c689f77d-a983-5bc3-b155-772969319d19"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"17.30.250","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/17.30.250","content_hash":"f30263ec5c733f1ba4494268b8060e9c64153b9eb1c538b39b63eda86cc6f813","heading":null,"ordinal":1,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:17.30.250:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:17.30.250:block:1","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/17.30.250","text":"(a) Danger to life and property due to flood damage;","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"00196300-bbb8-5b47-91f7-72fc6151a26a"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"17.30.250","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/17.30.250","content_hash":"a2a049f6a376c313b014ec521e0358dbfb12c34ec03d23421278c1e53f9dbff9","heading":null,"ordinal":2,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:17.30.250:section",